        <mxCell id="architecture-note" parent="arch-box" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F5F7;strokeColor=#7A869A;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=13;spacing=14;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;Core behavior:&lt;/b&gt; The create path obtains a unique code, commits the mapping, then warms Redis before returning 201. The read-heavy redirect path checks CDN/Redis first and reaches the sharded database only on a cache miss. Cache failure falls back to the durable store; database uniqueness remains the final collision guard." vertex="1">
